# .semgrepignore
# Excludes vendored/non-shipped trees from DevGuard SAST (semgrep) scans.
# gitignore-style patterns, read automatically by semgrep — no CLI flag exists
# for this in devguard-scanner v1.6.0 (verified via `devguard-scanner sast --help`).
#
# skills/        — vendored BMAD skill docs/scripts, not shipped application code
# deploy/        — example/recommended IaC (Terraform, Helm) for operators, not code we ship
# e2e/           — Playwright/Gherkin test fixtures (e.g. fake credentials, insecure-by-design samples)
# docs/          — story/architecture markdown, e.g. documented example bcrypt hashes for dev Dex users
# dev/           — local dev stack config (dev/dex/config.yaml example credentials, ADR-012)
# docker/        — e2e/dev-only nginx configs and CI Dockerfiles, not the shipped server image
# .github/       — mirror-only workflow config, not run on this GitLab-hosted repo
# _bmad-output/  — pipeline-generated epic artifacts/write-ups, not shipped code
# phoenix*.min.js — vendored Phoenix/Phoenix LiveView JS bundled into priv/static, not authored by us
# server/test/   — test fixtures (e.g. fake Twilio-key-shaped cross-signing test data)
skills/
deploy/
e2e/
docs/
dev/
docker/
.github/
_bmad-output/
server/priv/static/assets/phoenix*.min.js
server/test/
